<div class="fm-anti-root" data-testid="content-page-anti-slip-guide">
  <!-- Header Banner -->
  <header class="fm-anti-header">
    <div class="fm-anti-header-inner">
      <span class="fm-anti-eyebrow">Guide</span>
      <h1 class="fm-anti-title">Anti-Slip Guide</h1>
      <p class="fm-anti-subtitle">Underneath it all: what rug pads do, why they matter, and how to choose the right one.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="fm-anti-body-sec">
    <div class="fm-anti-body-inner">

      <!-- 1. What are anti-slip mats? -->
      <h2 class="fm-anti-h2">What are anti-slip mats?</h2>
      <p class="fm-anti-p">Anti-slip mats may not be the most thrilling topic, but don't underestimate them. They extend the life of your rugs, add cushioning, and prevent slips and falls. Here's a quick breakdown of what they do and how they help.</p>

      <!-- 2. Why you might want one -->
      <h2 class="fm-anti-h2">Why you might want one</h2>
      <ul class="fm-anti-ul">
        <li>Floor protection — a barrier between rug and floor</li>
        <li>Slip resistance — keeps rugs from sliding on hard floors</li>
        <li>Impact absorption — softer underfoot, easier on joints</li>
        <li>Prolonged rug lifespan — reduces friction wear</li>
        <li>Noise reduction — quieter footsteps in busy rooms</li>
        <li>Comfort underfoot — a subtle but noticeable difference</li>
      </ul>

      <!-- 3. Custom anti-slip mat, tailored to your rug -->
      <h2 class="fm-anti-h2">Custom anti-slip mat, tailored to your rug</h2>
      <p class="fm-anti-p">Your rug is more than décor — it's an investment. We offer custom rug pads cut to your rug's exact dimensions, so it sits flat and stays in place. Because when it comes to rugs, one size really doesn't fit all.</p>

      <!-- 4. Frequently asked -->
      <h2 class="fm-anti-h2">Frequently asked</h2>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">What are rug pads used for?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Rug pads prevent rugs from slipping, protect floors from scratches, and add cushioning. They also promote air circulation to help prevent moisture buildup, and make cleaning easier by acting as a barrier between the rug and the floor.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">What size rug pad do I need?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Match the pad to your rug's size and shape. Opt for an exact fit — or a slightly larger pad that can be trimmed. Non-slip pads should sit just inside the rug edge.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">Does the rug pad stick to the floor?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">No. Non-slip pads simply grip the floor so the rug stays in place, and can be removed at any time.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">Can you stitch my rug pad to my carpet?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">We don't recommend stitching a pad to your carpet — it can cause damage and make future cleaning or rearranging difficult.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">How do I clean rug pads?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Vacuum both sides regularly. Washable pads can be machine washed on a gentle cycle with mild detergent and air-dried. Non-washable pads can be spot-cleaned with mild detergent and a soft brush or cloth, or hand-washed in a bathtub with a thorough rinse.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">How much do rug pads cost?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Our rug pads are available at fixed, affordable pricing across sizes. For a custom cut, contact our team.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">Do rug pads make a carpet feel more plush?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Rug pads are primarily designed for slip resistance, floor protection, and rug stability. Some pads made from foam or felt can add a small amount of cushioning underfoot.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">Do rug pads work like anti-skid?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Yes. They have a grippy underside that adheres to the floor to keep the rug in place — important on hardwood and tile, where slipping is a real hazard.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">Do rug pads extend the life of a carpet?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">They can. By reducing wear, preventing slipping, adding cushioning, and improving air circulation, pads act as a protective barrier between the rug and the floor.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fm-anti-qa-block">
        <div class="fm-anti-qa-question">Do rug pads make a rug softer?</div>
        <p class="fm-anti-qa-answer">Pads aren't designed specifically to make a rug softer, but foam or felt pads can add a slightly softer feel underfoot.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</div>
